    {
      "title": "University courses covering Israel-Palestine should be audited, Julian Leeser tells royal commission",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/24/university-courses-covering-israel-palestine-should-be-audited-julian-leeser-tells-royal-commission-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Inquiry’s focus this week is on security for the Jewish community, with the MP telling the commissioner his son is afraid to attend synagogues and events</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The shadow education minister, Julian Leeser, has called for universities to undertake an audit of any classes that teach about the Jewish community, Israel or Palestine.</p><p>Appearing before the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/royal-commission-on-antisemitism-and-social-cohesion\">royal commission</a> into antisemitism and social cohesion on Friday, Leeser said he had been “very concerned” about antisemitism on university campuses and was not satisfied with how vice-chancellors had addressed the issue after the 7 October 2023 Hamas terrorist attack.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/24/university-courses-covering-israel-palestine-should-be-audited-julian-leeser-tells-royal-commission-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-24T08:30:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Julian Leeser says his son no longer feels safe at Jewish events – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/24/australia-news-live-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-labor-conference-gas-tax-gambling-reform-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australian exports sent to the US will be hit with a 12.5% tariff as the US president imposes levies on more than 80 nations.</p><p>The Trump administration unveiled the latest tranche of tariffs for countries over their “failure to impose and effectively enforce a prohibition on the importation of goods produced with forced labour”.</p><p><em><strong>This, in our view, makes no sense.</strong></em></p><p><em>Forced labour is definitely something which needs to be combated around the world, so we support that objective.</em></p><p><em>We absolutely need to see the strait of Hormuz be open and for freedom of navigation to happen there, for commercial shipping to be allowed through, and we very much call on Iran to allow that to be the case.</em></p><p><em>We need to see a restoration to the normal global fuel supply chain because it’s having a significant impact around the world.</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/24/australia-news-live-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-labor-conference-gas-tax-gambling-reform-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-24T08:23:43"
    },
    {
      "title": "Donald Trump hits Australian exports to US with new higher trade tariff over claims of ‘forced labour’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/24/donald-trump-hits-australian-exports-to-us-with-new-higher-trade-tariff-over-claims-of-forced-labour",
      "description": "<p>Australia’s trade minister, Don Farrell, says tariff regime is unjustified and inconsistent with free trade agreement with US</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/24/australia-news-live-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-labor-conference-gas-tax-gambling-reform-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Donald Trump has hit Australian exports with new trade tariffs, claiming the country is not doing enough to combat forced labour, but the Albanese government has demanded he remove them immediately.</p><p>The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/23/trump-administration-trade-tariffs\">United States announced on Friday morning</a> (AEST) that many Australian exports now attract a new 12.5% tariff as part of a broader regime affecting dozens of countries. However the Albanese government says Australia’s three largest export categories – including beef and gold – will avoid the tariff hit.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/24/donald-trump-hits-australian-exports-to-us-with-new-higher-trade-tariff-over-claims-of-forced-labour\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-24T07:04:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australian regulator TGA warns of ‘rare but severe’ eye disorder linked to GLP-1 drugs like Ozempic",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/24/tga-warning-gpl1-eye-disorder-drugs-ozempic-wegovy-mounjaro",
      "description": "<p>TGA says product information for some diabetes and weight loss drugs updated with warning of NAION disorder</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/24/australia-news-live-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-labor-conference-gas-tax-gambling-reform-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s medicines regulator has issued warnings for several type 2 diabetes and obesity-related treatments – including Ozempic and Mounjaro – over the potential to cause a “rare but severe” eye disorder that could lead to blindness.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.tga.gov.au/news/safety-updates/glp-1-ras-and-rare-vision-disorder\">The Therapeutic Goods Administration’s (TGA) warning</a> came after several GLP-1 RA medicines marketed in Australia as Ozempic, Wegovy and Mounjaro, among other products, were linked to 36 cases of the condition.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/24/tga-warning-gpl1-eye-disorder-drugs-ozempic-wegovy-mounjaro\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-24T06:39:09"
    },
